Package: python3-flag-attention
Architecture: all
Depends: python3:any, ${misc:Depends}, python3-pytest
# python3-pytest is a runtime Depends (not just for tests) because
# flag_attn/__init__.py imports flag_attn.testing → testing/piecewise.py
# which does `import pytest` at module scope. Upstream should lazy-import,
# but for now we keep the consumer install working.
# Triton (FlagOS-built or upstream) is NOT a hard Depends: the upstream
# python3-triton is too old (Ubuntu noble ships 2.0; PyPI is 2.4+), and the
# right install path for users is pip. python3-flagtree-nvidia is the only
# distro-distributable option, so we Recommend it.
Recommends: python3-flagtree-nvidia
Description: FlagAttention — memory-efficient attention operators (Triton)
 FlagAttention is a collection of memory-efficient attention operators
 implemented in the Triton language. It targets large-language-model
 training and inference workloads where the standard PyTorch attention
 path is memory-bound.
 .
 Triton (provided here by python3-flagtree-nvidia or upstream
 python3-triton) is required at runtime; without it the kernels
 cannot JIT-compile.
